
Case Study on OOP and Collections in java


Student marks lookup System

You are tasked with a Student marks lookup System. The system must store student names, student IDs as unique keys and corresponding object values. Each object should contains name, marks, grade.
the system should allow fast O(1) insertion, updates, deletion and look-ups.

Requirements:
1. Store records
   The system can store number of records dynamically.
   If a student roll number already exists update marks only(don't update other things even given)
2. Process Queries
  The Query should be
  1. Get <name> : Print details student if exists, if not exist raise exception student not found.
  2. Get <ID>: Print marks of the student with given ID. If student not exists raise exception student not found.
  3. Update <ID>: Given the student with ID, update his/her marks. If student not exist then insert new record.
  4. Remove<ID>: Remove the student from the collection. If student not exist raise student not found exception.
  5. Exists<ID>: Print true if student exists in the collection, otherwise false.